WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.950
In the 1500s, Catholics and Lutherans
condemned each other's teaching on how a

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.300
sinner is put right with God.

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.080
Then, on 31 October 1999, in Augsburg, the
two churches signed a joint declaration

4
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.900
on justification.

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:19.650
Yet one New Testament letter says
a person is justified by works,

6
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.710
and not only by faith.

7
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.630
Another says we are justified
by faith, apart from works.

8
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.070
So did the Reformers misread Paul?

9
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.540
And do Catholics really
think good deeds earn heaven?

10
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.340
In this mission, you'll see where the
churches stand on faith and works today.

11
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:40.970
Then you'll weigh up whether faith and
works are both part of justification.

12
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.630
Your mission: weigh up what
the churches teach about faith,

13
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.030
works and Paul.
